# Pinned commit SHAs for the chatbot's RAG corpus (internal/docindex/docs/),
# for every source that is NOT this repo. LiveReview's own docs/ subtree is
# NOT listed here - it's read straight from the working tree at sync time
# (see scripts/sync_docs_sources.sh), never fetched over the network.
#
# GitHub, not any developer's machine, is the source of truth: these SHAs
# are what actually gets embedded into the binary (dev builds, `make build`,
# and Docker images alike - see scripts/sync_docs_sources.sh). Bumping a
# value here is a deliberate, reviewable change, not something that happens
# automatically on every dev-server start.
#
# Checking for drift / bumping: see docs/docs-sources-pinning-plan.md, or
# run `make check-docs-sources` / `make update-docs-sources` /
# `make update-docs-sources-yes`.
#
# Whenever an agent commits a docs change in git-lrc or either wiki repo,
# it must bump the matching line below in the SAME task/commit - see the
# "Keeping scripts/docs_sources.env in Sync" section of AGENTS.md.
GIT_LRC_COMMIT=14584106823b1597e2097fca9ff42d2d18de5417
GIT_LRC_WIKI_COMMIT=a1bb17c392a46c1f3bf6cfad6396813ccf80a1a9
LIVEREVIEW_WIKI_COMMIT=b212da48de8ecacb167f562682d2a6491a1e327f
